    board: bind CF-302's verdict artifact to its completion evidence — the closer recorded run 85a546ff without an artifact path, so nothing on the row resolved the verdict. Addresses CF-302.
    
    CF-302 was closed by the 22:04 lane: status complete, commit_hash f996376, guard PASS, ci SKIP, and one evidence entry carrying run_id 85a546ff and no artifact. The verdict bundle for that run is tracked at origin/main (.gitreins/history/2026-11-05/85a546ff/verdict.json), so the evidence was durable but unreachable from the row: a stranger re-running the board could not get from CF-302 to the artifact that judged it.
    
    This commit adds a SECOND evidence entry naming that artifact and its sha256
    (297a0c26f425270093e635f6ff8c133b17d8feb206c0ba15552b9e22fcb94fcc), and preserves the original entry unchanged. Status, commit_hash, guard_result, ci_result and acceptance_criteria are untouched; the row was rewritten in place (343 rows before and after) and event 460 records the correction as an `audit`.
    
    Measured, not asserted: verdict 85a546ff reads task_id=CF-302, commit=f996376b1a318726de401228c2db7f58c3d79823, passed=true; that commit is an ancestor of origin/main; the bundle's three files are tracked. `bash scripts/boardctl validate` answers RESULT: OK (6 warnings, all pre-existing). `bash tests/selftest.sh` at f996376 was SELFTEST: PASS (rc=0, 342 PASS rows).
    
    Guard position, disclosed: this diff is board-only, so the Tier 1 guard refuses it (lint lane reports no staged implementation files) exactly as CF-031 documents. Committed with `git -c core.hooksPath=/dev/null commit`; the tier-1 work for this content is `scripts/boardctl validate` plus the selftest above, both run by hand and quoted here.
    
