 {"id": "CF-303", "title": "land-node-branch.sh exits 0 on an already-landed commit WITHOUT running the gate command", "status": "pending", "priority": "P1", "complexity": "medium", "reasoning": "The already-landed path returns success before the gate runs: measured with `--gate-cmd 'exit 99'`, exit 0. So a commit landed earlier by another route, or landed and then broken, is reported as landed-clean without the one check that would have caught it.", "acceptance_criteria": "1. The gate runs on every path that reports success, including already-landed.\n2. A fixture with a red gate on an already-landed commit exits non-zero.\n3. The skip, if any is kept, is printed as a named row.", "created_at": "2026-11-05T17:51:18Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-05T17:51:18Z"}
 {"id": "CF-304", "title": "load_lane_config.py has no read-only mode — every invocation writes six live lanes, including --check and --dry-run", "status": "pending", "priority": "P1", "complexity": "medium", "reasoning": "The script's whole job is to write: measured, any invocation issues UPDATEs against the scheduler DB, and `--dry-run --check` writes anyway. There is no mode that reports what it WOULD change. Combined with a CFG whose namespaces contradict fleet.toml:1918 (all six lanes set to `code-factory` while the fleet config says otherwise), a diagnostic run silently repoints live lanes — and the write is schema-legal because every namespace exists.", "acceptance_criteria": "1. A read-only mode exists and is the default; writing requires an explicit flag.\n2. --dry-run prints the exact UPDATE set and performs none of it.\n3. A fixture against a copy of the DB proves zero writes for every non-writing mode.", "created_at": "2026-11-05T17:51:18Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-05T17:51:18Z"}
 {"id": "CF-305", "title": "lane_target.py accepts an ambiguous primary whose own name ends in a satellite suffix, rejecting nothing", "status": "pending", "priority": "P1", "complexity": "medium", "reasoning": "family_key (:450) splits `notes-docs` from its own satellite `notes-docs-qa`, so two lanes on two different valid roots both pass: `0 rejected, 2 accepted`, exit 0. The same pair named `notes`/`notes-qa` correctly exits 4. Measured across the live fleet read-only: 174 such never-compared pairs, 173 with differing repo_url, 0 currently with two valid roots — latent, and reachable by adding one satellite.", "acceptance_criteria": "1. A primary is identified by its own row, not by suffix-stripping its name.\n2. The fleet scan reports the 174 never-compared pairs instead of passing them.\n3. Fixtures for both namings produce the same verdict.", "created_at": "2026-11-05T17:51:18Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-05T17:51:18Z"}
